---
description: Job application tracker — architecture and version constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

# Stack (do not substitute versions)
Java 21, Spring Boot 4.1.1, Spring Framework 7, Spring Security 7,
Jackson 3, PostgreSQL, jjwt 0.12.6, Maven.
Frontend: React 18 + Vite, plain axios, React Router. No Redux, no Next.js.

# Hard rules
- Spring Security 7. SecurityFilterChain @Bean with lambda DSL only.
  NEVER WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter, antMatchers, authorizeRequests,
  or .and() chaining — all removed. Nothing is implicit: declare every
  behavior explicitly.
- CSRF is enabled by default in Security 7. This is a stateless JWT API,
  so csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable()) is required.
- Jackson 3, not Jackson 2. Do not write custom JsonSerializer /
  JsonDeserializer or use ObjectMapper constructors directly.
- jjwt 0.12.x API only. Building: Jwts.builder().subject(x).signWith(key).compact()
  Parsing: Jwts.parser().verifyWith(key).build().parseSignedClaims(token).getPayload()
  NEVER setSigningKey(String), parserBuilder(), or Jwts.parser().parseClaimsJws().
- Every repository method that touches user data takes userId:
  findByIdAndUserId, findAllByUserId. NEVER a bare findById on Application
  or StatusEvent — that is an IDOR.
- Controllers return DTOs (Java records). Entities are never serialized.
- current_status on Application is written ONLY by StatusService.transition().
  No other service or controller may set it.
- Use constructor injection. No @Autowired on fields.
- Do not add dependencies, Flyway, Liquibase, MapStruct, or Docker Compose
  unless I ask.

# Package layout
com.jidnesh.jobtracker.{config,security,user,auth,application,status,exception}

# Data model
User (id, email UK, passwordHash, createdAt)
Application (id, userId FK, company, roleTitle, location, source, appliedOn,
             currentStatus, notes, createdAt, updatedAt)
StatusEvent (id, applicationId FK, status, note, occurredAt)
Status enum: APPLIED, ONLINE_ASSESSMENT, INTERVIEW, OFFER, REJECTED, WITHDRAWN

StatusEvent is the source of truth. Application.currentStatus is a denormalized
read optimization updated in the same @Transactional method that inserts the
event.
